    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Year Unknown is a short &quot;walking sim&quot; with a branching narrative. It takes ~1 hour to complete.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore <strong>The Library</strong>,<strong> </strong>a megastructure the size of the universe, filled with all of humanity's knowledge. To guide you are two Artificial Intelligences, built to process its massive collection of information.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But something else is calling you - a distress call from the center of the universe. The stagnant universe is breaking down, and there may be no way to save it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2565520/extras/e672291fab5653a39cb3423093452dfc.avif?t=1748703000\" width=616 height=198 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore brutalist landscapes, and find terminals to talk to two AI. Both have different thoughts and opinions, and might tell you different things. Fortunately, you have control: choose which AI to talk to, what to tell them or leave out, and ultimately, decide who you agree with.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Accessibility</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Includes the following accessibility options:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Text size adjustment</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >OpenDyslexic as an alternative font</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Text-to-speech</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Option to reduce the motion of certain effects and sequences</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Note: This game <strong>does not</strong> contain content from a generative AI. The AI in the game are written characters.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Year Unknown is a short &quot;walking sim&quot; with a branching narrative. It takes ~1 hour to complete.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore <strong>The Library</strong>,<strong> </strong>a megastructure the size of the universe, filled with all of humanity's knowledge. To guide you are two Artificial Intelligences, built to process its massive collection of information.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But something else is calling you - a distress call from the center of the universe. The stagnant universe is breaking down, and there may be no way to save it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2565520/extras/e672291fab5653a39cb3423093452dfc.avif?t=1748703000\" width=616 height=198 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore brutalist landscapes, and find terminals to talk to two AI. Both have different thoughts and opinions, and might tell you different things. Fortunately, you have control: choose which AI to talk to, what to tell them or leave out, and ultimately, decide who you agree with.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Accessibility</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Includes the following accessibility options:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Text size adjustment</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >OpenDyslexic as an alternative font</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Text-to-speech</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Option to reduce the motion of certain effects and sequences</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Note: This game <strong>does not</strong> contain content from a generative AI. The AI in the game are written characters.</p>",
